md @VERSION@ for Linux — the portable archive
=========================================

md is a Markdown editor with a live preview beside the text. This archive
holds the same files as the .deb and .rpm packages, in one folder:

  bin/md                   the program
  share/md/                its examples and preview engines; bin/md finds
                           them here, wherever the folder is
  share/applications/      the desktop entry
  share/icons/             the icon, in 13 sizes
  share/metainfo/          the software-centre description
  share/mime/packages/     the Markdown, PlantUML, Graphviz and TextPack types
  share/man/man1/md.1.gz   the manual page
  share/doc/md/            README, CHANGELOG, PRIVACY, the licences
                           (copyright) and an AppArmor profile (see below)

Requirements
------------

The libraries of Ubuntu 26.04 or Fedora 44, or later: GTK 4.22, libadwaita
1.9, WebKitGTK 6.0 2.52, GLib 2.88 and glibc 2.39 or newer, and the fonts
Nimbus Mono PS (URW base35) and Liberation Mono. On those systems:

  Ubuntu:  sudo apt install libgtk-4-1 libadwaita-1-0 libwebkitgtk-6.0-4 \
               fonts-urw-base35 fonts-liberation
  Fedora:  sudo dnf install gtk4 libadwaita webkitgtk6.0 \
               urw-base35-nimbus-mono-ps-fonts liberation-mono-fonts

Where the .deb or .rpm fits, prefer it: the package manager brings all of
this, and on Ubuntu the .deb also installs the AppArmor profile.

Run it
------

  tar -xzf md-@VERSION@-linux-*.tar.gz
  md-@VERSION@/bin/md

To install it for yourself, with md in the app grid and offered for Markdown
files:

  cp -r md-@VERSION@/bin md-@VERSION@/share ~/.local/
  update-desktop-database ~/.local/share/applications
  update-mime-database ~/.local/share/mime

and make sure ~/.local/bin is on your PATH. To remove it, delete what was
copied: ~/.local/bin/md, the rich and examples folders in ~/.local/share/md
(not the whole folder: md keeps your unsaved drafts in its drafts folder),
~/.local/share/doc/md, ~/.local/share/man/man1/md.1.gz, and the files named
me.nettrash.md.* under ~/.local/share.

Ubuntu 24.04 and later
----------------------

The preview runs in WebKit's sandbox, which needs a user namespace, and
Ubuntu lets a program create one only when an AppArmor profile allows it. The
.deb installs that profile for /usr/bin/md. For this archive, copy
share/doc/md/apparmor-profile to /etc/apparmor.d/md, change /usr/bin/md in
it to the full path of bin/md, and load it:

  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/md

If the sandbox cannot start, md says so and quits; it never runs the preview
without it.

https://nettrash.me/linux/md/support.html
